Among architectural modifications, replacing C2f modules with traditional CSP blocks reduced mAP@0.5 by 1.9% (0.995 vs. 0.976), while reverting to a coupled detection head reduced precision by 2.7% (0.999 vs. 0.963). Anchor-free detection reduced model size by 3.1% without performance loss. For loss functions, replacing CIoU with standard IoU reduced mAP@0.5−0.95 by 2.1% (0.942 vs. 0.921); removing label smoothing reduced precision by 0.8% (0.999 vs. 0.991); and equal loss weighting reduced mAP@0.5 by 1.3%. Data augmentation had the largest single impact: complete removal caused a 7.6% precision degradation (0.999 vs. 0.923), while using basic augmentation only (without Mosaic or MixUp) reduced mAP@0.5 by 1.4%. Training with 30 epochs instead of 80 reduced mAP@0.5 by 1.0% (0.995 vs. 0.985), confirming that the 80-epoch budget is justified without evidence of overfitting. Table 8 Ablation study results for YOLOv8s Configuration Precision Recall mAP@0.5 mAP@0.5:0.95 FPS Full YOLOv8s (baseline) 0.999 1.000 0.995 0.942 196 Without C2f modules 0.971 0.983 0.976 0.901 218 Without decoupled head 0.963 0.975 0.968 0.889 209 IoU instead of CIoU 0.988 0.994 0.989 0.921 196 Without label smoothing 0.991 0.997 0.991 0.928 196 No augmentation 0.923 0.946 0.931 0.842 196 Basic augmentation only 0.976 0.989 0.981 0.903 196 30 epochs (vs. full 80) 0.981 0.992 0.985 0.912 196 All variants trained under identical conditions: 80 epochs (except where noted), batch size 16, Adam optimiser ( \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
